From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eglantine PS5 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: a fragment barrier ends the render pass only when a draw needs it (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone or in the lichii-cpu order.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 161, commit 3985ac21c6, and PR 184, commit 60e565c440 (a pending barrier
survives unrelated draws), GPL-3.0-or-later. PR 161 was still open on 6 Nov; PR 184 is merged.
Lichii had the deferred path for MoltenVK already; this core had none of it, so the scheduler state,
writes_storage and SamplesRenderTarget come along.

EDEN_NX2_DEFER_FRAGMENT_BARRIER=1: FRAGMENT_BARRIER inside a render pass marks the pass. The next
draw ends it only if it samples a bound render target, or if the pass wrote storage. Unset, or with
no pass active, it is the old call.

Added here: DrawTexture does not go through ConfigureImpl, so it takes a pending barrier at once.
The colour feedback copies (ReplaceColorFeedbackViews) end the pass themselves. writes_storage and
NoteRenderPassStores sit a few lines lower than in Lichii, to stay clear of the lines
fable-mesh-compute-0181 changes; this patch applies before or after that one.

Why it may matter on the console: PR 161 counts about 5,900 render passes a second in Ocarina on a
PC. The barrier count per frame comes from the game, so it should carry over; the fps numbers do
not. Each pass end costs the Vulkan worker a barrier and the GPU a drain. run61 shows only 3.4 ms of
a 42 ms frame on the fence, so a frame rate gain is not expected unless the worker is the limit.

Risk: a texture view that aliases a render target through a different image is not seen by
SamplesRenderTarget. Compare the picture with the switch on and off.

Pool memory: none.

Checked: PS5-target syntax compile of the derived files (vulkan_rasterizer.cpp,
vk_graphics_pipeline_cost.cpp, vulkan_scheduler.cpp, vk_texture_cache_cost.cpp): 0 errors.
prepare-vulkan-port.py reports the same anchors as core16 and carries the edits. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
index 96a819983b..1f166d0f6d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
@@ -313,6 +313,13 @@ GraphicsPipeline::GraphicsPipeline(
     uses_descriptor_buffer = builder.CanUseDescriptorBuffer() && descriptor_buffer_ring.IsValid();
     descriptor_set_layout =
         builder.CreateDescriptorSetLayout(uses_push_descriptor, uses_descriptor_buffer);
+    const auto any_written = [](const auto& descriptors) {
+        return std::ranges::any_of(descriptors, [](const auto& desc) { return desc.is_written; });
+    };
+    writes_storage = std::ranges::any_of(stage_infos, [&](const Shader::Info& info) {
+        return info.stores_global_memory || any_written(info.storage_buffers_descriptors) ||
+               any_written(info.image_descriptors) || any_written(info.image_buffer_descriptors);
+    });
     if (uses_descriptor_buffer) {
         descriptor_buffer_layout = builder.MakeDescriptorBufferLayout(*descriptor_set_layout);
         if (!descriptor_buffer_ring.CanAllocate(descriptor_buffer_layout.size)) {
@@ -670,8 +677,12 @@ bool GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureImpl(bool is_indexed) {
     {
         Profile::Scope scope{Profile::Zone::RenderTargets};
         texture_cache.UpdateRenderTargets(false);
-        texture_cache.CheckFeedbackLoop(
-            std::span<const VideoCommon::ImageViewInOut>{views.data(), views.size()});
+        const std::span<const VideoCommon::ImageViewInOut> view_span{views.data(), views.size()};
+        texture_cache.CheckFeedbackLoop(view_span);
+        if (scheduler.HasFragmentBarrier() &&
+            (scheduler.RenderPassHasStores() || texture_cache.SamplesRenderTarget(view_span))) {
+            scheduler.RequestOutsideRenderPassOperationContext();
+        }
     }
     if (IsBuilt() && !pipeline) {
         return false;
@@ -733,6 +744,9 @@ bool GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureDraw(const RescalingPushConstant& rescaling,
             build_condvar.wait(lock, [this] { return is_built.load(std::memory_order::relaxed); });
         });
     }
+    if (writes_storage) {
+        scheduler.NoteRenderPassStores();
+    }
     const bool is_rescaling{texture_cache.IsRescaling()};
     const bool update_rescaling{scheduler.UpdateRescaling(is_rescaling)};
     const bool bind_pipeline{scheduler.UpdateGraphicsPipeline(this)};
